# Cloudflare Pages response headers. Static export can't emit a next.config
# headers() block, so the baseline security headers live here and apply to every
# path: clickjacking, MIME sniffing, and referrer leakage. (No CSP — the inline
# theme-init script would need a per-request nonce/hash, and a misconfigured CSP
# failing closed is a worse risk than its marginal benefit on a static site.)
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  # Lock down powerful APIs the calculator never uses, and isolate the browsing context.
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Ask caches to revalidate the service worker so a new deploy is detected promptly. NOTE:
# Cloudflare Pages currently serves /sw.js with its own multi-hour max-age regardless of this
# rule, so prompt update detection is actually guaranteed by registering the worker with
# updateViaCache: "none" (components/ServiceWorker.tsx), which fetches sw.js past the HTTP cache
# on every update check. This rule states the intent and takes effect if that override is lifted.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
